As you imply, {selma'o} ({se cmavo}, after all, although the online diction=
ary didn't turn it up) is only for cmavo, which is the way CLL uses it in t=
he grammar.=A0 {cmene} on the other hand is all over the place, but strictl=
y applies only to string of cmevla (as we would now say) in the grammar.=A0=
 It appears that, in trying to avoid murdering English, ala JCB, for jargon=
, we have ended up murdering Lojban itself.=A0 Personally, I prefer English=
, even twisted, to languages which we don't really understand to begin with=
.




